        "summary": "no-mistakes puts a local git proxy in front of your real remote. Push to no-mistakes instead of origin, and it spins up a disposable worktree, runs an AI-driven validation pipeline, forwards the branch to the configured push target only after every check passes, and opens a clean PR automatically. Non-blocking - the pipeline runs in an isolated worktree without disrupting your work. Agent-agnostic - claude, codex, rovodev, opencode, pi, or acp: via acpx. Agent-native - /no-mistakes lets your coding agent do a task and gate it, or gate existing committed work: it runs the pipeline, has the pipeline apply safe fixes, and escalates the rest to you. Human stays in charge - auto-fix or review fin",
